  "text": "proprium.dominica-xxi-post-pentecosten-offertorium",
  "about": "The offertorium of the formulary “21st Sunday after Pentecost” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "In the land of Uz there was a man named Job, guileless and upright, one who feared God. Satan asked for him, that he might test him; and power over his goods and over his flesh was given to him by the Lord; and he destroyed all his possessions, and his children; he also wounded his flesh with a grievous sore." }
  },
